2086
01:16:21,877 --> 01:16:23,378
That was intense.

2087
01:16:23,946 --> 01:16:25,614
That was stressful.

2088
01:16:26,014 --> 01:16:28,250
THE INTENSE SEAFOOD ROUND IS NOW OVER

2089
01:16:28,317 --> 01:16:30,252
That could've gone so wrong at the end.

2090
01:16:30,319 --> 01:16:34,523
Now, both dishes are finished
for the Gyeongsang-do sisters.

2091
01:16:35,524 --> 01:16:36,925
SIGHS

2092
01:16:36,992 --> 01:16:39,962
My heart almost stopped in this round.

2093
01:16:40,028 --> 01:16:42,464
<i>Right? He almost</i>
<i>couldn't make the cocktail.</i>

2094
01:16:43,265 --> 01:16:46,034
I really wanted to try it,

2095
01:16:46,602 --> 01:16:49,104
-so it would've been…
-"What if we can't try it?"

2096
01:16:49,171 --> 01:16:51,974
<i>-</i>It took less than a minute.
-Please, the cocktail!

2097
01:16:52,040 --> 01:16:54,676
First, try Chef Hyun-suk's dish.

2098
01:16:55,611 --> 01:16:59,581
CHOI HYUN-SUK'S TAKE ON CHINESE CUISINE,
A SEAFOOD PARTY

2099
01:17:02,117 --> 01:17:06,655
CUTLASSFISH, SHRIMP, STALKED SEA SQUIRT,
SCALLOPS, AND FLYING FISH ROE

2100
01:17:08,590 --> 01:17:11,593
CHEF CHOI HYUN-SUK'S
LET'S GO CUTLASSFISH A STAR

2101
01:17:12,427 --> 01:17:14,162
TA-DA

2102
01:17:14,229 --> 01:17:15,797
It's piping hot.

2103
01:17:16,031 --> 01:17:16,999
SNIFF

2104
01:17:17,065 --> 01:17:18,533
Whoa.

2105
01:17:18,600 --> 01:17:20,535
-Earlier…
-It smells like shrimp innards.

2106
01:17:20,602 --> 01:17:23,071
Yes, it smells like seafood innards.

2107
01:17:23,138 --> 01:17:26,108
Toward the end,
he poured a huge batch of flying fish roe.

2108
01:17:26,174 --> 01:17:27,776
Let me take a picture. One second.

2109
01:17:28,877 --> 01:17:31,013
GASPING…

2110
01:17:31,413 --> 01:17:32,648
WAIT!

2111
01:17:33,415 --> 01:17:34,850
She's just like me.

2112
01:17:34,916 --> 01:17:35,817
I can't wait.

2113
01:17:37,519 --> 01:17:38,520
You two

2114
01:17:38,587 --> 01:17:40,722
seem rather aggressive when you see food.

2115
01:17:40,989 --> 01:17:42,457
THE SISTERS CHANGE IN FRONT OF FOOD

2116
01:17:42,524 --> 01:17:43,825
They're not listening.

2117
01:17:43,892 --> 01:17:44,960
They're not listening at all.

2118
01:17:45,761 --> 01:17:46,895
They don't care about the show.

2119
01:17:46,962 --> 01:17:48,463
IN PERFECT HARMONY

2120
01:17:48,530 --> 01:17:52,934
She's like the older sister sharing food
on her way to find refuge.

2121
01:17:53,001 --> 01:17:54,670
-She's forcing her to eat.
-In a war.

2122
01:17:54,736 --> 01:17:56,538
-"You have to eat this now!"
-"Eat while you can."

2123
01:17:56,872 --> 01:17:59,041
WERE YOU TWO AROUND BACK THEN?

2124
01:17:59,608 --> 01:18:01,810
SOLEMN

2125
01:18:01,877 --> 01:18:03,278
Cutlassfish fritters.

2126
01:18:03,345 --> 01:18:04,680
Does it smell like the sea?

2127
01:18:04,746 --> 01:18:07,382
Very much. It's such a pleasant smell.

2128
01:18:07,749 --> 01:18:09,551
EAT UP, GIRLS

2129
01:18:10,519 --> 01:18:12,554
It's Chef Hyun-suk's dish,

2130
01:18:13,388 --> 01:18:14,656
in Chinese-style.

2131
01:18:14,723 --> 01:18:17,592
He added shrimp heads, stalked sea squirt,
<i>mala xiang guo </i>sauce, and more.

2132
01:18:17,659 --> 01:18:20,562
NAKYOUNG TRIES
THE SEAFOOD FRITTER IN ONE BITE

2133
01:18:21,029 --> 01:18:23,165
Why do I feel like their parent?

2134
01:18:23,231 --> 01:18:24,499
It's so heartwarming.

2135
01:18:24,566 --> 01:18:27,069
It's literally rich.

2136
01:18:27,135 --> 01:18:28,336
The shrimp heads.

2137
01:18:28,403 --> 01:18:29,438
Mmm.

2138
01:18:29,504 --> 01:18:31,506
<i>The richness of the shrimp heads.</i>

2139
01:18:31,573 --> 01:18:34,142
-Does it taste strong?
-Very much.

2140
01:18:34,209 --> 01:18:36,278
He ground the shrimp heads.

2141
01:18:36,344 --> 01:18:37,713
BIBI TRIES THE FRITTER TOO

2142
01:18:37,779 --> 01:18:39,147
Is it still hot?

2143
01:18:39,214 --> 01:18:41,049
Just as Jung-hwan had mentioned,

2144
01:18:41,116 --> 01:18:42,317
it's not just one flavor.

2145
01:18:42,384 --> 01:18:45,554
-It's hard to explain.
-Yes, it's hard to explain.

2146
01:18:45,620 --> 01:18:48,590
Does it seem closer to Chinese cuisine?

2147
01:18:48,657 --> 01:18:50,525
-It does.
-If I had to choose one, yes.

2148
01:18:50,592 --> 01:18:51,993
If I had to choose.

2149
01:18:52,060 --> 01:18:55,063
<i>-But the </i>mala <i>flavor isn't too strong.</i>
<i>-It's not?</i>

2150
01:18:55,130 --> 01:18:56,965
The cutlassfish goes
really well with this.

2151
01:18:57,032 --> 01:18:58,333
-Shrimp?
-Yes.

2152
01:18:58,400 --> 01:19:00,068
They don't hurt each other.

2153
01:19:00,135 --> 01:19:01,303
The taste of shrimp heads is strong,

2154
01:19:01,369 --> 01:19:04,706
and cutlassfish tastes clean,

2155
01:19:05,273 --> 01:19:07,676
so it felt like shrimp heads
would overpower the other.

2156
01:19:07,743 --> 01:19:09,644
But the flavor is there.
I like the dredge too.

2157
01:19:10,479 --> 01:19:11,680
It's perfect.

2158
01:19:11,747 --> 01:19:13,415
It sat in the soup,

2159
01:19:13,482 --> 01:19:17,385
-so it became soft and chewy.
-Yes.

2160
01:19:17,452 --> 01:19:19,654
So this… Wow.

2161
01:19:19,721 --> 01:19:22,357
The moment you eat
a bite of boneless cutlassfish,

2162
01:19:22,424 --> 01:19:23,792
there's just something.

2163
01:19:23,859 --> 01:19:25,260
-Happiness, right?
-Also, he mixed

2164
01:19:25,327 --> 01:19:28,230
<i>shrimp with pork fat, remember?</i>

2165
01:19:28,296 --> 01:19:32,167
So that probably added a bouncy texture.

2166
01:19:32,734 --> 01:19:33,969
There's stalked sea squirt here too.

2167
01:19:34,035 --> 01:19:35,837
-You did?
-Yes.

2168
01:19:35,904 --> 01:19:37,873
<i>She said she liked them, so he added some.</i>

2169
01:19:38,173 --> 01:19:39,641
WILL IT GO WELL
WITH THE SHRIMP HEAD SAUCE?

2170
01:19:39,708 --> 01:19:41,777
It's made to their taste.

2171
01:19:42,778 --> 01:19:43,812
Stalked sea squirt.

2172
01:19:43,879 --> 01:19:45,981
You need it.
You need the stalked sea squirt.

2173
01:19:46,948 --> 01:19:48,650
It's so delicious.

2174
01:19:48,717 --> 01:19:50,185
Isn't it still hot?

2175
01:19:50,252 --> 01:19:51,386
It's not.

2176
01:19:51,453 --> 01:19:52,788
I think

2177
01:19:52,854 --> 01:19:54,823
they just can't feel heat and spiciness.

2178
01:19:54,890 --> 01:19:56,391
LAUGHING

2179
01:19:56,458 --> 01:19:57,859
Both heat and spiciness?

2180
01:19:59,628 --> 01:20:00,962
Excuse me. Are you two watching TV?

2181
01:20:01,263 --> 01:20:02,564
GUILTY

2182
01:20:03,598 --> 01:20:05,634
They're like siblings

2183
01:20:05,700 --> 01:20:08,670
watching TV and making comments.

2184
01:20:08,737 --> 01:20:10,172
"They eat so well."

2185
01:20:10,238 --> 01:20:12,140
CAN'T HEAR THEM

2186
01:20:12,207 --> 01:20:14,009
-But they're so small.
-Right?

2187
01:20:14,276 --> 01:20:15,977
IN A TRANCE

2188
01:20:16,211 --> 01:20:17,712
"It must be hot, but they can eat it."

2189
01:20:17,779 --> 01:20:18,780
That was steamy.

2190
01:20:18,847 --> 01:20:21,049
She's finishing everything.

2191
01:20:21,116 --> 01:20:23,118
-She must've been starving.
-Right?

2192
01:20:23,185 --> 01:20:24,519
Maybe all day long.

2193
01:20:24,586 --> 01:20:26,888
I haven't been to many restaurants,

2194
01:20:26,955 --> 01:20:30,192
but this tasted like a plate of luxury.

2195
01:20:30,258 --> 01:20:32,661
I've never had anything like this.

2196
01:20:32,727 --> 01:20:33,762
She's the poor female lead type.

2197
01:20:34,296 --> 01:20:35,997
STALKED SEA SQUIRT OVER FLOWERS

2198
01:20:36,064 --> 01:20:38,266
The rich guy's taste,
the poor girl's taste.

2199
01:20:38,600 --> 01:20:40,302
SHARING THE RICH TASTE
WITH THE POOR SISTERS

2200
01:20:40,368 --> 01:20:42,938
It hits me toward the end.

2201
01:20:43,004 --> 01:20:45,874
-The <i>mala </i>flavor.
-The <i>mala </i>flavor.

2202
01:20:45,941 --> 01:20:46,975
Toward the end.

2203
01:20:47,042 --> 01:20:48,577
Was that intentional?

2204
01:20:48,643 --> 01:20:52,080
If I added more <i>mala </i>sauce
just because they liked it,

2205
01:20:52,147 --> 01:20:54,749
it would've killed
the briny flavor in the seafood.

2206
01:20:54,816 --> 01:20:56,051
-I see.
-Right.

2207
01:20:56,117 --> 01:20:58,920
So I added just a bit for the numbness
and tried to bring out

2208
01:20:58,987 --> 01:21:00,021
the seafood's flavor more.

2209
01:21:00,255 --> 01:21:01,790
I SEE!

2210
01:21:01,857 --> 01:21:03,992
Less for the food, more for his uniform.

2211
01:21:04,059 --> 01:21:05,994
It could've gone in there,

2212
01:21:06,061 --> 01:21:07,629
but I chose to put it here instead.

2213
01:21:08,630 --> 01:21:09,464
He sacrificed himself.

2214
01:21:09,531 --> 01:21:11,399
-That was his intention.
-He took the blow.

2215
01:21:11,466 --> 01:21:15,003
He couldn't let everything
go into the dish.

2216
01:21:15,070 --> 01:21:17,839
Next, Chef Jong-won's dish.

2217
01:21:18,473 --> 01:21:22,510
SPECIAL MELJEOT SAUCE AND ESCARGOT PASTA

2218
01:21:23,879 --> 01:21:27,515
ARE WE IN ULSAN OR FRANCE?

2219
01:21:28,650 --> 01:21:30,819
AND STALKED SEA SQUIRT?

2220
01:21:31,653 --> 01:21:35,190
CHEF SON JONG-WON'S
BIBI, NAKYOUNG, AS REAL AS EVER

2221
01:21:35,757 --> 01:21:37,726
May I come and shake

2222
01:21:37,792 --> 01:21:38,860
the cocktail?

2223
01:21:38,927 --> 01:21:41,796
Please shake them for a bit
next to the fridge owners.

2224
01:21:42,197 --> 01:21:43,265
SHAKE

2225
01:21:44,132 --> 01:21:45,700
-Let me shake it.
-He's shaking it.

2226
01:21:46,301 --> 01:21:50,405
SOJU MARTINI IN SEA SQUIRT GLASSES

2227
01:21:50,472 --> 01:21:52,407
There's stalked sea squirt inside.

2228
01:21:52,474 --> 01:21:53,842
-Thank you.
-How did he make this?

2229
01:21:55,110 --> 01:21:57,946
-He put stalked sea squirts on a skewer.
-He did.

2230
01:21:58,013 --> 01:22:00,081
-It's a martini.
-Martini.

2231
01:22:00,148 --> 01:22:03,919
It's usually made with olives.

2232
01:22:03,985 --> 01:22:06,755
It reminds me of stone sea pineapples

2233
01:22:06,821 --> 01:22:08,423
-you can eat by the sea.
-Sea pineapple shot.

2234
01:22:08,490 --> 01:22:10,392
It'll probably taste like that.

2235
01:22:10,458 --> 01:22:12,527
-Sea pineapple shot.
-So it reminds you of that.

2236
01:22:12,594 --> 01:22:14,362
-It'll feel like that.
-I see.

2237
01:22:14,429 --> 01:22:15,997
A toast.

2238
01:22:16,064 --> 01:22:17,198
BEING POLITE TO EACH OTHER?

2239
01:22:17,265 --> 01:22:18,500
OH, RIGHT!

2240
01:22:18,566 --> 01:22:20,035
They both love soju.

2241
01:22:21,670 --> 01:22:23,638
What's it like? Is it bad?

2242
01:22:23,705 --> 01:22:24,606
This is…

2243
01:22:25,640 --> 01:22:28,009
-What is this?
-"What is this?"

2244
01:22:28,076 --> 01:22:29,911
Yes, what is this?

2245
01:22:30,578 --> 01:22:31,413
A cocktail.

2246
01:22:31,479 --> 01:22:32,681
Well, yes.

2247
01:22:32,747 --> 01:22:35,450
-Does it taste weird?
-It doesn't.

2248
01:22:35,517 --> 01:22:37,953
Why does alcohol go so well
with sea squirt?

2249
01:22:38,019 --> 01:22:41,623
Right. But it doesn't
really taste like alcohol.

2250
01:22:41,690 --> 01:22:44,025
But it still tastes like alcohol.

2251
01:22:44,092 --> 01:22:47,228
And the smell of stalked sea squirt
suddenly hits you.

2252
01:22:47,295 --> 01:22:48,530
Yet it feels so good.

2253
01:22:48,596 --> 01:22:49,798
It tastes so pleasant.

2254
01:22:49,864 --> 01:22:52,634
But seriously, this is a huge wonder.

2255
01:22:52,701 --> 01:22:54,202
When you make martinis,

2256
01:22:54,269 --> 01:22:56,071
there are olives in it,
which are quite salty

2257
01:22:56,137 --> 01:22:59,574
making the drink smoother
while adding depth.

2258
01:22:59,641 --> 01:23:00,775
It's the same concept here.

2259
01:23:00,842 --> 01:23:04,079
After watching films like the 007 series,
I had always wanted to try martinis,

2260
01:23:04,145 --> 01:23:07,482
but when I ordered them,
they tasted awful to me.

2261
01:23:07,549 --> 01:23:10,452
-But this one is so good.
-It is?

2262
01:23:10,518 --> 01:23:11,553
I can just enjoy this.

2263
01:23:11,619 --> 01:23:13,421
She's already done.

2264
01:23:13,488 --> 01:23:15,256
Does it taste like the real deal?

2265
01:23:15,323 --> 01:23:17,625
I want more of this.

2266
01:23:17,692 --> 01:23:18,893
It was that good?

2267
01:23:18,960 --> 01:23:19,961
One more drink.

2268
01:23:20,028 --> 01:23:22,831
-Ask him for more.
-It was so good.

2269
01:23:22,897 --> 01:23:25,400
You can mix the red cap
with the white in two to one ratio.

2270
01:23:25,467 --> 01:23:27,769
-Red and white?
-So it's kind of strong.

2271
01:23:27,836 --> 01:23:28,970
It's high in proof.

2272
01:23:29,037 --> 01:23:32,574
-It's strong.
-Also, it's made with olive juice,

2273
01:23:32,640 --> 01:23:36,311
so instead of that,
I used the heart of palm juice.

2274
01:23:36,378 --> 01:23:38,346
I added a dash of lemon too,

2275
01:23:38,413 --> 01:23:41,449
trying to bring out
the cucumber-like flavor.

2276
01:23:41,516 --> 01:23:42,584
It's like magic.

2277
01:23:42,650 --> 01:23:45,787
-He's like a magician.
-I knew it.

2278
01:23:45,854 --> 01:23:47,589
Please try the dish now.

2279
01:23:47,889 --> 01:23:48,890
PASTA IN ESCARGOT SHAPE

2280
01:23:48,957 --> 01:23:50,558
Escargot.

2281
01:23:50,625 --> 01:23:51,459
POP!

2282
01:23:51,726 --> 01:23:53,194
NO WAY

2283
01:23:53,261 --> 01:23:54,863
-It really looks like escargot.
-It does.

2284
01:23:56,831 --> 01:23:57,999
Right away?

2285
01:23:58,066 --> 01:23:59,701
That pasta is shaped like a conch.

2286
01:23:59,768 --> 01:24:00,602
It's good.

2287
01:24:00,835 --> 01:24:01,669
THEIR HAPPY MUKBANG

2288
01:24:01,736 --> 01:24:03,738
"It's good."

2289
01:24:03,805 --> 01:24:05,140
I didn't know if I should serve

2290
01:24:05,206 --> 01:24:07,609
two shrimps or three,

2291
01:24:07,675 --> 01:24:09,110
but I thought I should serve just one.

2292
01:24:09,177 --> 01:24:10,011
What?

2293
01:24:10,779 --> 01:24:13,948
Then we can see BIBI eating the tail.

2294
01:24:14,149 --> 01:24:15,050
OH, THAT?

2295
01:24:15,116 --> 01:24:16,851
-That one.
-NaKyoung, leave me the tail.

2296
01:24:17,419 --> 01:24:18,686
HE PLANNED FOR THIS SIGHT TO UNFOLD?

2297
01:24:18,753 --> 01:24:20,121
It was intentional?

2298
01:24:20,188 --> 01:24:22,924
-It was intentional.
-NaKyoung eats the meat.

2299
01:24:22,991 --> 01:24:24,059
-That was it.
-What's it like?

2300
01:24:25,360 --> 01:24:26,661
Why is this sweet?

2301
01:24:26,728 --> 01:24:28,530
It tastes like sweet potato.

2302
01:24:28,596 --> 01:24:29,898
It tastes like sweet potato?

2303
01:24:30,131 --> 01:24:31,232
ONE SECOND

2304
01:24:32,333 --> 01:24:33,835
-As little meat as possible.
-Hey.

2305
01:24:33,902 --> 01:24:34,836
RIGHT!

2306
01:24:34,903 --> 01:24:37,272
SORRY! HAD SOME MEAT LEFT

2307
01:24:37,338 --> 01:24:38,273
Just the tail for BIBI.

2308
01:24:39,074 --> 01:24:40,675
-Isn't it sweet?
-Why?

2309
01:24:40,742 --> 01:24:43,344
-Is it?
-It really is sweet.

2310
01:24:43,411 --> 01:24:45,180
-Why is it sweet?
-Why is it sweet?

2311
01:24:45,246 --> 01:24:48,016
I had left it in alcohol for a bit.

2312
01:24:48,917 --> 01:24:50,919
-It tastes like sweet potato.
-It does, right?

2313
01:24:50,985 --> 01:24:54,022
-What's this?
-You can scoop some

2314
01:24:54,089 --> 01:24:56,324
-and put it on the pasta.
-It's for the pasta.

2315
01:24:56,391 --> 01:24:59,360
Jong-won has become quite brazen.

2316
01:24:59,427 --> 01:25:02,263
-Why?
-He burnt the other shrimp.

2317
01:25:02,330 --> 01:25:03,498
I see.

2318
01:25:03,565 --> 01:25:05,733
RUNNING AWAY

2319
01:25:05,800 --> 01:25:08,570
When Hyun-suk
took the shrimps out for him,

2320
01:25:08,636 --> 01:25:11,506
one was burnt and completely charred.

2321
01:25:12,006 --> 01:25:14,476
-He turned that into this?
-He spun a story.

2322
01:25:15,944 --> 01:25:17,245
You're funny these days.

2323
01:25:17,312 --> 01:25:18,646
"Share one with each other."

2324
01:25:18,713 --> 01:25:19,881
PASTA WITH MELJEOT SAUCE

2325
01:25:21,449 --> 01:25:22,283
What's it like?

2326
01:25:22,350 --> 01:25:23,485
"Who made this?"

2327
01:25:23,551 --> 01:25:24,853
Who made this?

2328
01:25:24,919 --> 01:25:26,087
-What is this?
-The sauce?

2329
01:25:26,154 --> 01:25:28,323
-Coconut.
-Right?

2330
01:25:28,857 --> 01:25:30,258
Did you use <i>meljeot </i>for this?

2331
01:25:30,325 --> 01:25:32,193
That and water parsley.

2332
01:25:32,260 --> 01:25:34,462
-Coconut. I can taste the coconut.
-Yes.

2333
01:25:34,529 --> 01:25:37,765
It tastes completely different
when I had it with the sauce

2334
01:25:37,832 --> 01:25:39,601
compared to when I had it by itself.

2335
01:25:39,667 --> 01:25:40,869
It's so good.

2336
01:25:41,703 --> 01:25:44,839
The umami of <i>meljeot </i>hits me first,

2337
01:25:44,906 --> 01:25:48,109
then it wraps up pleasantly
with the coconut flavor.

2338
01:25:49,277 --> 01:25:52,380
-It must taste clean.
-Yet it retained both flavors.

2339
01:25:52,447 --> 01:25:54,415
-Isn't it so good?
-That sauce.

2340
01:25:54,482 --> 01:25:56,351
-It must be good.
-It's so good.

2341
01:25:56,417 --> 01:25:58,386
So this sauce is different, right?

2342
01:25:58,453 --> 01:25:59,521
It's so good.

2343
01:25:59,721 --> 01:26:00,688
TWO LEFT

2344
01:26:00,755 --> 01:26:02,557
Scallops and shrimp.

2345
01:26:02,624 --> 01:26:04,993
-And pasta.
-I had nothing to eat today.

2346
01:26:05,059 --> 01:26:06,294
They eat so well.

2347
01:26:06,361 --> 01:26:08,363
The portion wasn't big,

2348
01:26:08,796 --> 01:26:09,998
so they share it.

2349
01:26:10,064 --> 01:26:13,234
Was the pasta good?
The conch-shaped pasta?

2350
01:26:13,301 --> 01:26:15,136
-It's so good.
-Is it?

2351
01:26:15,203 --> 01:26:17,338
Wait a second.

2352
01:26:17,405 --> 01:26:20,108
-Our viewers have nothing to eat.
-They got nothing.

2353
01:26:20,175 --> 01:26:21,009
-Oh, no.
-What?

2354
01:26:21,075 --> 01:26:22,911
-Nothing?
-It's time to decide.

2355
01:26:22,977 --> 01:26:24,946
-What? Nothing?
-Wait, there's nothing?

2356
01:26:25,013 --> 01:26:25,914
They'll decide.

2357
01:26:25,980 --> 01:26:28,283
Are these seats supposed to be miserable?

2358
01:26:28,650 --> 01:26:29,851
PICKING UP STUFF

2359
01:26:29,918 --> 01:26:31,019
Is this our punishment?

2360
01:26:31,085 --> 01:26:32,187
I have a bit left.

2361
01:26:32,253 --> 01:26:35,156
-There is some left.
-We'll let them try it.

2362
01:26:35,223 --> 01:26:37,559
Is there anything else?
She can't have shrimp.

2363
01:26:38,126 --> 01:26:39,794
-Do you not eat them?
-I'm allergic.

2364
01:26:39,861 --> 01:26:43,364
-Everything is made with shrimp.
-It's made with shrimp heads.

2365
01:26:43,698 --> 01:26:44,933
THE SHOCKING TRUTH

2366
01:26:44,999 --> 01:26:45,934
I'll take it.

2367
01:26:46,000 --> 01:26:47,869
Thank you.

2368
01:26:47,936 --> 01:26:49,470
What about Jong-won?

2369
01:26:49,537 --> 01:26:51,005
She can't eat them.

2370
01:26:51,072 --> 01:26:52,507
-But Nathan can eat some.
-He's fine.

2371
01:26:52,574 --> 01:26:53,908
-Really?
-Nathan's fine.

2372
01:26:53,975 --> 01:26:56,344
-Confiscated.
-Give it up.

2373
01:26:56,411 --> 01:26:57,912
-Why?
-It's for the guest.

2374
01:26:57,979 --> 01:26:59,080
That's mine!

2375
01:27:01,716 --> 01:27:02,550
TEARFUL

2376
01:27:02,617 --> 01:27:04,152
It's as if he's here alone.

2377
01:27:05,887 --> 01:27:07,689
First, Chef Hyun-suk's dish.

2378
01:27:07,755 --> 01:27:09,357
Can I at least smell it?

2379
01:27:11,326 --> 01:27:12,660
She won't let him eat it alone.

2380
01:27:12,727 --> 01:27:13,661
Aren't you allergic?

2381
01:27:17,465 --> 01:27:19,500
What's this thing that's popping?

2382
01:27:19,567 --> 01:27:21,169
-Flying fish roe.
-Flying fish roe.

2383
01:27:21,236 --> 01:27:23,972
-That adds a fun texture.
-Flying fish roe.

2384
01:27:25,473 --> 01:27:26,674
ALL CLEARED!

2385
01:27:26,741 --> 01:27:28,042
He eats so well.

2386
01:27:28,276 --> 01:27:30,411
WAILING

2387
01:27:35,083 --> 01:27:37,252
Teasing Patricia as much as he can.

2388
01:27:37,318 --> 01:27:38,820
TEASING HER ON ANOTHER LEVEL

2389
01:27:38,886 --> 01:27:41,289
AS ELEGANTLY AS POSSIBLE

2390
01:27:44,492 --> 01:27:45,760
YUM

2391
01:27:47,528 --> 01:27:48,496
Is it good?

2392
01:27:48,563 --> 01:27:50,398
Wait, this sauce.

2393
01:27:50,465 --> 01:27:51,299
WHAT IS THIS?

2394
01:27:51,366 --> 01:27:52,500
It's unique.

2395
01:27:52,567 --> 01:27:54,202
Yes, it's really unique.

2396
01:27:54,269 --> 01:27:55,103
Mmm.

2397
01:27:55,169 --> 01:27:58,373
-I love the bite too.
-The texture?

2398
01:27:58,439 --> 01:27:59,741
It reminds me of <i>tteokbokki.</i>

2399
01:27:59,807 --> 01:28:01,276
Yes, it's like <i>tteokbokki,</i>

2400
01:28:01,342 --> 01:28:05,113
-but with rosé sauce.
-Rosé <i>tteokbokki.</i>

2401
01:28:05,313 --> 01:28:06,648
IMMERSED

2402
01:28:09,617 --> 01:28:11,252
BOILING INSIDE

2403
01:28:12,086 --> 01:28:14,355
THE ELDEST ARE ON THE SAME FREQUENCY

2404
01:28:14,422 --> 01:28:16,391
He finishes every single bite.

2405
01:28:16,457 --> 01:28:18,393
ALL CLEARED!

2406
01:28:18,459 --> 01:28:20,261
Thank you. That was delicious.

2407
01:28:20,995 --> 01:28:22,697
It's now time to choose.

2408
01:28:22,764 --> 01:28:24,666
<i>Press one for Jong-won</i>

2409
01:28:25,400 --> 01:28:26,834
<i>and two for Hyun-suk.</i>

2410
01:28:27,902 --> 01:28:29,137
Make your decision

2411
01:28:29,704 --> 01:28:31,205
and press the button.

2412
01:28:32,106 --> 01:28:33,708
They both pressed the button.

2413
01:28:34,275 --> 01:28:36,511
I wonder how they voted.

2414
01:28:37,545 --> 01:28:38,579
Whoa!

2415
01:28:38,646 --> 01:28:39,947
Are they on the same page?

2416
01:28:40,515 --> 01:28:41,582
They're on the same page.

2417
01:28:42,917 --> 01:28:43,918
Two to zero.

2418
01:28:43,985 --> 01:28:45,186
Twice as humiliating.

2419
01:28:45,253 --> 01:28:48,623
-Exactly. How unfortunate.
-Yes.

2420
01:28:48,690 --> 01:28:50,825
The humiliation.

2421
01:28:51,359 --> 01:28:52,560
FEELING BAD

2422
01:28:52,627 --> 01:28:54,629
Which one became the winner?

2423
01:28:54,696 --> 01:28:57,432
-Let's find out the result.
-So?

2424
01:28:57,498 --> 01:28:59,200
Hyun-suk versus Jong-won.

2425
01:28:59,267 --> 01:29:01,269
Gyeongsang-do Sisters' Soul Food.

2426
01:29:01,336 --> 01:29:03,905
Jong-won, who's currently
the only one in first place.

2427
01:29:03,971 --> 01:29:06,474
But Hyun-suk had won
more rounds against him.

2428
01:29:06,541 --> 01:29:09,977
Who did BIBI and NaKyoung choose?

2429
01:29:10,044 --> 01:29:11,279
Who is it?

2430
01:29:11,913 --> 01:29:15,650
Who won the seafood round?

2431
01:29:15,717 --> 01:29:18,419
-The two good-looking chefs' round.
-Who's the winner?

2432
01:29:18,486 --> 01:29:20,221
Who is it?

2433
01:29:20,288 --> 01:29:22,023
SON JONG-WON WINS

2434
01:29:22,090 --> 01:29:23,057
It was Jong-won.

2435
01:29:23,324 --> 01:29:27,161
CHEF SON JONG-WON'S
BIBI, NAKYOUNG, AS REAL AS EVER WINS

2436
01:29:27,228 --> 01:29:29,464
Jong-won beats Hyun-suk

2437
01:29:29,530 --> 01:29:31,232
and takes the star.

2438
01:29:31,299 --> 01:29:32,800
It wasn't simply food.

2439
01:29:32,867 --> 01:29:37,138
It was a mix of cultures between
my hometown and something foreign

2440
01:29:37,205 --> 01:29:38,906
coming together within me,

2441
01:29:38,973 --> 01:29:40,775
which gives birth
to someone awesome like me.

2442
01:29:41,142 --> 01:29:42,343
AGREED

2443
01:29:42,410 --> 01:29:43,711
It was a new experience.

2444
01:29:43,778 --> 01:29:44,979
-I see.
-It was fun.

2445
01:29:46,447 --> 01:29:49,384
Jong-won, you now have 12 stars.

2446
01:29:50,351 --> 01:29:53,488
I wasn't paying attention to the oil,

2447
01:29:53,554 --> 01:29:55,590
and the temperature had risen too high.

2448
01:29:55,656 --> 01:29:59,727
-But Hyun-suk let me use his.
-That's true.

2449
01:29:59,794 --> 01:30:03,698
-That was how I could finish.
-And he got the shrimps out too.

2450
01:30:03,765 --> 01:30:05,833
I couldn't have done it without him.

2451
01:30:05,900 --> 01:30:07,268
It was for his little brother.

2452
01:30:07,335 --> 01:30:08,870
He sacrificed himself.

2453
01:30:08,936 --> 01:30:10,805
-And his outfit.
-And his outfit.

2454
01:30:10,872 --> 01:30:12,807
This is a huge loss.

2455
01:30:12,874 --> 01:30:14,675
I may have become torn apart,

2456
01:30:14,742 --> 01:30:16,744
tattered, and crumpled,

2457
01:30:16,811 --> 01:30:19,147
but I just wanted to see Jong-won do well
through my sacrifice.

2458
01:30:19,447 --> 01:30:20,715
ABOUT TO CRY

2459
01:30:22,316 --> 01:30:24,185
THAT WAS GOOD!

2460
01:30:24,252 --> 01:30:26,954
Were you a bit hesitant
when you got the shrimp out?

2461
01:30:27,021 --> 01:30:29,557
I didn't even hesitate for a second.

2462
01:30:29,624 --> 01:30:31,292
-I knew it.
-Whoa.

2463
01:30:31,359 --> 01:30:33,928
"Should I get this one out
and put it in the hotter oil?"

2464
01:30:36,063 --> 01:30:37,665
THE ELDEST IS ALSO THE FUNNIEST

2465
01:30:37,732 --> 01:30:39,367
Please put the star on him.

2466
01:30:39,434 --> 01:30:41,602
This is his 12th star.

2467
01:30:41,669 --> 01:30:44,205
He now has 12 wins in the sole 1st place.

2468
01:30:44,939 --> 01:30:48,209
He continues to widen the gap.

2469
01:30:49,410 --> 01:30:51,779
The hottest siblings
in the entertainment business.

2470
01:30:51,846 --> 01:30:53,848
You bought a car for Patricia?

2471
01:30:54,115 --> 01:30:55,049
NO WAY

2472
01:30:55,349 --> 01:30:56,584
TOTALLY SMUG

2473
01:30:56,651 --> 01:30:58,119
But the monthly payment is on me.

2474
01:30:58,453 --> 01:30:59,454
WHAT DO YOU MEAN?

2475
01:30:59,520 --> 01:31:00,455
I didn't pay it off entirely.

2476
01:31:00,521 --> 01:31:02,023
I don't want to spoil her.

2477
01:31:02,256 --> 01:31:03,458
THE BROTHER'S THOUGHTFUL TAKE

2478
01:31:03,524 --> 01:31:05,226
I see some awful comments

2479
01:31:05,293 --> 01:31:07,662
asking if I'm Patricia
whenever I put on wigs.

2480
01:31:07,728 --> 01:31:09,530
His eyes are kind of glazed.

2481
01:31:09,597 --> 01:31:12,600
He always goes around looking like this.

2482
01:31:12,667 --> 01:31:13,868
Here are the orders.

2483
01:31:13,935 --> 01:31:15,570
The dishes to die for.

2484
01:31:15,636 --> 01:31:16,871
DISHES TO DIE FOR?

2485
01:31:16,938 --> 01:31:18,473
Are you trying to say goodbye to her?

2486
01:31:18,539 --> 01:31:20,007
One of us has to go.

2487
01:31:20,308 --> 01:31:21,542
FRIGHTENINGLY SWEET DISHES

2488
01:31:21,609 --> 01:31:23,077
FOR THE SIBLINGS
OUT FOR EACH OTHER'S NECK

2489
01:31:23,511 --> 01:31:24,779
A PILE OF SUGAR

2490
01:31:24,846 --> 01:31:26,113
-Whoa.
-Whoa.

2491
01:31:26,180 --> 01:31:27,582
HERE TO SKYROCKET YOUR BLOOD SUGAR

2492
01:31:27,648 --> 01:31:28,983
Something smells sweet.

2493
01:31:29,050 --> 01:31:30,585
These are sweet dishes.

2494
01:31:31,152 --> 01:31:32,286
-Whoa.
-Look at Nathan.

2495
01:31:32,720 --> 01:31:33,788
HAVE THE SIBLINGS FAINTED?

2496
01:31:33,955 --> 01:31:35,223
STRUCK BY THE BLOOD SUGAR SPIKE

2497
01:31:35,389 --> 01:31:36,657
NEXT UP, SPICINESS!

2498
01:31:36,958 --> 01:31:38,593
FULL OF CHEONGYANG PEPPERS

2499
01:31:38,726 --> 01:31:41,028
THROWING IN EXTREMELY SPICY THINGS

2500
01:31:41,095 --> 01:31:42,063
BLECH!

2501
01:31:42,263 --> 01:31:43,264
THE SPICIEST DISH YET?

2502
01:31:43,331 --> 01:31:44,665
It's extremely spicy!

2503
01:31:44,732 --> 01:31:45,733
You'd die.

2504
01:31:45,800 --> 01:31:46,667
I'm not dead.

2505
01:31:46,868 --> 01:31:48,269
THE TWO WITH A HIGH SPICE TOLERANCE

2506
01:31:49,003 --> 01:31:50,905
-This isn't spicy?
-Is something wrong with me?

2507
01:31:50,972 --> 01:31:52,306
-I was surprised.
-It's so good.

2508
01:31:52,373 --> 01:31:54,408
WHICH DISH DID THE SIBLINGS FALL FOR?

2509
01:31:55,543 --> 01:31:57,712
<i>-It's insane.</i>
<i>-It's so good, though.</i>

2510
01:31:57,778 --> 01:31:59,213
Can you two get closer?

2511
01:31:59,280 --> 01:32:02,083
Closer.

2512
01:32:02,683 --> 01:32:06,153
-Are we getting paid extra for this?
-I was going to ask.

2513
01:32:15,596 --> 01:32:20,368
Subtitle translation by:
Eunsook Youn
